From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@Averys-MacBook-Air.local>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:13:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] MSL: transform feedback from geometry shaders run as
 mesh stages

- A geometry shader with Xfb takes a spvXfbGeometry state (xfb_geometry_buffer_index):
  in count mode it records the primitives of each input primitive and invocation
  (ordered by instance, input primitive, invocation) and emits none; in capture
  mode each completed primitive is written, in the strip's order, at the
  exclusive prefix sum of the counts plus its index, if it fits in every buffer.
  The first invocation records written / needed primitives and bytes.
- The payload's primitive fields (ID, instance, primitive count) come before the
  vertexes, whose layout the two stages declare separately.
- Geometry shader helper functions return their values (only the entry point
  returns void), and only gl_InvocationID and gl_PrimitiveIDIn are passed from
  the mesh wrapper (per-vertex builtins come with the stage input).
